      "content": "To explain to stakeholders, consider this: Vertical scaling involves upgrading existing servers or hardware to increase their processing power, memory, or storage capacity, typically to handle increased workload or traffic. In contrast, horizontal scaling, also known as scaling out, involves adding more servers or resources to an existing infrastructure to distribute the load, thus increasing overall processing power and capacity. This approach allows for more granular flexibility and control over the system's performance.",
